cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PolicyEngine Macro"
message: >-
  If you use PolicyEngine Macro — the integration layer, the archived data
  vintages, or a figure from the site — in academic or published work, please
  cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmadi
    given-names: Vahid
    affiliation: PolicyEngine
  - family-names: Ghenis
    given-names: Max
    affiliation: PolicyEngine
  - name: PolicyEngine
    website: "https://policyengine.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PolicyEngine/macro"
url: "https://policyengine-macro.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  An open platform for answering economic and public-policy questions with
  transparent, reproducible models. PolicyEngine Macro places household
  microsimulation, macroeconometric scenarios, structural VAR shock
  identification, heterogeneous-agent dynamics and long-run overlapping
  generations analysis behind a common discovery and run surface — a CLI and
  a hosted MCP server — alongside an append-only point-in-time archive of the
  official statistics the models are conditioned on.
keywords:
  - economic modelling
  - public policy
  - microsimulation
  - macroeconomics
  - structural VAR
  - overlapping generations
  - heterogeneous agents
  - point-in-time data
  - reproducible research
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"

# Not yet claimed: `doi` and `identifiers`. A DOI becomes available once
# releases are minted and the repository is connected to Zenodo; see
# CONTRIBUTING.md. Adding a placeholder DOI would break every citation that
# copied it.
#
# Each model class carries its own upstream citation. Citing this repository
# credits the integration, the archive and the site — not the underlying
# models. When a result depends on a specific model, cite that model's own
# paper as well; the per-model references live under `papers/`.
